## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time, multi-tenant safety workflow on GCP, including data boundaries and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub, Dataflow
- Content moderation: Vision API, text models, DLP
- Multi-tenant isolation: per-tenant datasets/buckets/projects
- Exactly-once semantics and deduplication
- Observability: Cloud Monitoring, Logging, Error Reporting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow DoFn: deduplicate by eventId
class DedupeFn extends DoFn {
  @ProcessElement
  public void process(@Element Event e, OutputReceiver<Event> out, StateAccessor state) {
    String id = e.eventId;
    if (!state.read().contains(id)) {
      state.write(id);
      out.output(e);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate idempotency and monitor data skew across tenants?
- How would you test failover to another region with minimal data loss?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests familiarity with GCP primitives for multi-tenant secrets, security isolation, API design, and basic caching/observability, suitable for a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- Secret Manager with per-tenant secrets and IAM isolation
- Cloud Run security and API key authentication
- Lightweight cache to reduce Secret Manager calls (60s)
- Observability via Cloud Logging and Monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();

async function accessSecretVersion(name) {
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({ name });
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate API keys and enforce revocation?
- How would you validate secret updates and cache invalidation?

